{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a thought-provoking film that explores the complexities of the human mind, the intricacies of relationships, and the cutthroat world of technology and innovation. directed by david fincher, the movie is a riveting portrayal of the rise of facebook and its founder, mark zuckerberg.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, being dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright (played by rachelissa). this rejection sparks a chain of events that leads to the creation of facemash, a website that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university.\n\nundeterred, mark teams up with his twin brothers, cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), and their business partner, divya narendra (played by maximiliano hernandez), to create a new website called harvard connect. however, mark soon becomes disenchanted with the project and decides to create his own social networking site, which he calls \"thefacebook\".\n\nas facebook gains popularity, mark becomes increasingly obsessed with its success, often at the expense of his relationships with his friends and family. the film explores the complexities of mark's character, portraying him as a brilliant, yet awkward and introverted individual who is driven by a desire for success and recognition.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its portrayal of the relationships between the characters. the dynamic between mark and his friend, eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), is particularly well-developed, as they navigate the ups and downs of their friendship amidst the rapid growth of facebook. the film also explores the complicated relationships between mark and the winklevoss twins, who are portrayed as entitled and arrogant, yet also sympathetic and relatable.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy, adding to the overall tension and unease that pervades the movie. the cinematography is sleek and modern, capturing the fast-paced and dynamic world of technology and innovation.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that raises important questions about the nature of success, friendship, and identity. it's a movie that will resonate with anyone who has ever felt like an outsider, or who has ever been driven by a passion or obsession. with its talented cast, clever script, and masterful direction, the social network is a must-see film that will leave viewers thinking long after the credits roll.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.9773347973823547}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0004104725376237184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.011048096232116222}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " thought", "logprob": -1.5990114212036133}, {"token": "-prov", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oking", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.036613818258047104}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0015041239093989134}, {"token": " explores", "logprob": -1.3174192905426025}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " complexities", "logprob": -0.26206615567207336}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0009390473715029657}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.3455899953842163}, {"token": " human", "logprob": -0.05462611839175224}, {"token": " mind", "logprob": -0.06179908290505409}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.038163281977176666}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.7270503044128418}, {"token": " intricacies", "logprob": -1.434798002243042}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " relationships", "logprob": -0.7415679097175598}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {